<h2 id="cost">Accuracy and inference cost</h2>
<figure><img src="accuracy-cost.svg" alt="Mean family accuracy versus mean API response cost">
<figcaption>Models with complete question coverage and a recorded charge for every selected response.
<a href="accuracy-cost.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="accuracy-cost.pdf">PDF</a> ·
<a href="accuracy-cost.png">PNG</a></figcaption></figure>
<p>Cost is the mean recorded charge for one selected response per question, including prompt, reasoning
and answer tokens. Correct, incorrect and truncated responses all count. Charges reflect the routes,
prices and cache discounts in effect during collection. We use the saved
<a href="https://openrouter.ai/docs/cookbook/administration/usage-accounting">OpenRouter usage records</a>;
<a href="https://openrouter.ai/support">credits are denominated in USD</a>.</p>
<p>This measures response inference cost, not total experiment spending: probes, failed or superseded
attempts, credit-purchase fees and hosting overhead are excluded. Locally served models have no measured
infrastructure cost in this archive. Missing charges remain unknown; they are never treated as zero.
Incomplete runs and models with missing charges are omitted from the plot.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Costed / returned / planned</th>
<th>Known response charges (USD)</th><th>Complete panel (USD)</th><th>Mean per question (USD)</th>
</tr></thead><tbody>
{% for row in metrics %}<tr><th>{{ row.label }}</th>
<td>{{ row.costed_responses }} / {{ row.returned }} / {{ row.planned }}</td>
<td>{{ '%.4f'|format(row.known_response_cost_usd) if row.known_response_cost_usd is not none else 'Unavailable' }}</td>
<td>{{ '%.4f'|format(row.panel_response_cost_usd) if row.panel_response_cost_usd is not none else 'Unavailable' }}</td>
<td>{{ '%.4f'|format(row.mean_response_cost_usd) if row.mean_response_cost_usd is not none else 'Unavailable' }}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
